ar: 10 daily record highs, no daily record lows","records":"Tupelo has nearly stopped setting record lows","change":"Tupelo's days and nights have warmed since 1986","rain":"Tupelo has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 54\u00b0F was the 16th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 97 since 1930, the coolest since 2022.","t_yest":"November 13: cooler than 83% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>54\u00b0F</strong> was the 16th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 97 since 1930, the coolest since 2022. The normal high for the date is 64\u00b0F, and the record is 84\u00b0F (1955). The low of <strong>33\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Tupelo has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Tupelo's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Tupelo has set <strong class=\"sig\">36 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 102 that chance alone would give, and <strong>116 record highs</strong>, close to the 103 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (83). Tupelo's all-time high is 109\u00b0F, on July 29, 1930.","t_chg":"Tupelo's days and nights have warmed since 1986","p_chg":"Across 87 complete years: Tupelo's average low shows no clear change: +0.14\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.00 to +0.27) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. Tupelo's average high shows no clear change: \u22120.01\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.13 to +0.10) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.61\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.29 to +0.94) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.76\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.34 to +1.19). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months; June fell.","t_rain":"Tupelo has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Tupelo's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.80 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.03 to +1.56), about +7.6 inches since 1930. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 57.7 inches a year. The wettest year was 1991 (81.05 in); the driest, 1943 (34.55 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 10 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}